{"id":"seir","name":"Seir","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:seir"],"types":[{"type":"person","from":"UBS: Names of People"},{"type":"group","from":"UBS: Names of Groups"},{"type":"place","from":"UBS: Names of Locations"}],"standing":"single-index","indexes":["nave"],"thin":false,"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Seir","text":"Rough; hairy. (1.) A Horite; one of the “dukes” of Edom (Gen. 36:20-30). (2.) The name of a mountainous region occupied by the Edomites, extending along the eastern side of the Arabah from the south-eastern extremity of the Dead Sea to near the Akabah, or the eastern branch of the Red Sea. It was originally occupied by the Horites (Gen. 14:6), who were afterwards driven out by the Edomites (Gen. 32:3; 33:14, 16). It was allotted to the descendants of Esau (Deut. 2:4, 22; Josh. 24:4; 2 Chr. 20:10; Isa. 21:11; Exek. 25:8). (3.) A mountain range (not the Edomite range, Gen. 32:3) lying between the Wady Aly and the Wady Ghurab (Josh. 15:10)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H8165","lemma":"שֵׂעִיר","xlit":"Sêʻîyr","gloss":"Seir, a mountain of Idumaea and its aboriginal occupants, also one in…","kjv":"Seir","count":19,"share":0.61},{"strong":"H2022","lemma":"הַר","xlit":"har","gloss":"a mountain or range of hills","kjv":"hill, mount, promotion","count":8,"share":0.26},{"strong":"H4057","lemma":"מִדְבָּר","xlit":"midbâr","gloss":"a pasture","kjv":"desert, south, speech, wilderness","count":4,"share":0.13},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":13,"share":0.42},{"strong":"H3427","lemma":"יָשַׁב","xlit":"yâshab","gloss":"to sit down","kjv":"abide, continue, dwell, ease self","count":5,"share":0.16}],"verses":["Gen.14.6","Gen.32.3","Gen.33.14","Gen.33.16","Gen.36.8","Gen.36.9","Gen.36.20","Gen.36.21","Gen.36.30","Num.24.18","Deut.1.2","Deut.2.1","Deut.2.4","Deut.2.5","Deut.2.12","Deut.2.22","Deut.33.2","Josh.11.17","1Chr.1.38"